# DLL / STL trust model

Living: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-14-base-root-hybrid-design.md` §DLL / STL trust model.  
Diagram: `docs/superpowers/diagrams/dll-stl-trust.html`.

## Boundaries

| Class | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| **A** 仓内产品 DLL（同 `out/<config>`、同 `/MD(d)`） | STL **allowed** across modules |
| **B** `content/public` | Lean signatures; no drive-by public thickening |
| **C** 插件 / glang ext / GetProcAddress | **No** `std::string` / `vector` / STL by value on the wire |
| **D** 第三方预编译 | Isolate / stub; do not mix heaps or CRT |

## Do

- Keep product CRT dynamic (`static_link_crt=false`). Debug stems `*_d.dll`; never mix with Release stems in one gen root.
- Prefer `COMPONENT_EXPORT(NAME)` + GN `IS_NAME_IMPL` for **new** modules; keep existing `*_EXPORT` when editing.
- Treat export macros as **link visibility**, not public API.
- On C boundaries: opaque handles, C buffers, or serialize; create/destroy on the owning side.
- Run / respect `build/tools/check_dll_homogeneity.py` after product link (stem rules + `SMARTGIS_BUILD_ID` marker).
- When changing a shared in-image layout, bump the matching `#pragma detect_mismatch` token (`abi_guard.h` / type-local in the header) in the **same** change.
- Call / keep `base::verify_product_dll_build_ids()` at product process start (after DLL search path setup).

## Don’t

- Don’t pass STL across plugin / script / foreign DLL edges.
- Don’t `#pragma comment` import libs when `COMPONENT_BUILD` is off (static component build).
- Don’t enable `/MT` for product modules.
- Don’t throw C++ exceptions across DLL or plugin boundaries.
- Don’t invent a second CRT or a second STL for product DLLs.
- Don’t use SEH / hot-path exception swallow as a substitute for build-id or detect_mismatch consistency.
